REGIONAL REGULATION OF BANYUMAS REGENCY

NUMBER 3 OF 2015

CONCERNING

IMPLEMENTATION OF PROTECTION

FOR VICTIMS OF GENDER-BASED VIOLENCE AND CHILDREN

BY THE GRACE OF ALMIGHTY GOD

REGENT OF BANYUMAS,

Considering : a. that all forms of violent acts, especially gender-based violence and violence against children constitute violations of human rights and crimes against human dignity;

b. that victims of gender-based violence and violence against children in the Region continue to increase;

c. that victims of violence need to be protected in their self-respect and dignity and guaranteed their right to life in accordance with their nature and disposition without discrimination;

d. that based on Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection and Law Number 23 of 2004 concerning Elimination of Domestic Violence, the Regional Government together with the community is obliged to undertake prevention, protection, and recovery efforts for victims of gender-based violence and violence against children;

e. that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a, letter b, letter c, and letter d it is necessary to stipulate a Regional Regulation concerning the Implementation of Protection for Victims of Gender-Based Violence and Children;

In view of 1. Article 18 paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;

2. Law Number 13 of 1950 concerning the Establishment of Regency Regions within Central Java Province;

3. Law Number 39 of 1999 concerning Human Rights (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1999 Number 165, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3886);

4. Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2002 Number 109, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4235);

5. Law Number 13 of 2003 concerning Manpower (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2003 Number 39, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4279);

6. Law Number 23 of 2004 concerning Elimination of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2004 Number 95, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number

7. Law Number 13 of 2006 concerning Protection of Witnesses and Victims (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2006 Number 64, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4635);

8. Law Number 21 of 2007 concerning Eradication of the Criminal Act of Trafficking in Persons (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2007 Number 58, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4720);

9. Law Number 11 of 2009 concerning Social Welfare (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2009 Number 12, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4976);

10. Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2014 Number 244 Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5587) as amended by Government Regulation in Lieu of Law Number 2 of 2014 concerning Amendment to Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2014 Number 246, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5589);

11. Government Regulation Number 4 of 2006 concerning Implementation and Cooperation in Recovery of Victims of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2006 Number 15, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 64);

12. Government Regulation Number 9 of 2008 concerning Procedures and Mechanisms for Integrated Services for Witnesses and/or Victims of the Criminal Act of Trafficking in Persons (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2008 Number 22, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4818);

13. Regional Regulation of Central Java Province Number 03 of 2009 concerning Implementation of Protection for Victims of Gender-Based Violence and Children (Regional Gazette of Central Java Province of 2009 Number 3, Supplement to the Regional Gazette of Central Java Province Number 20);

With Mutual Approval

REGIONAL HOUSE OF REPRESENTATIVES OF BANYUMAS REGENCY, and

REGENT OF BANYUMAS,

HAS DECIDED:

To stipulate : REGIONAL REGULATION CONCERNING IMPLEMENTATION OF PROTECTION FOR VICTIMS OF GENDER-BASED VIOLENCE AND CHILDREN.

Article 32

(1) Every victim of gender-based and child violence shall have the right to: a. obtain protection for personal safety, family and property, and be free from threats related to information that will be, is being, or has been provided; b. participate in the process of selecting and determining the form of protection and security support;

c. be free from incriminating questions;

d. obtain information regarding case developments and court decisions;

e. obtain complaint services, health services, social rehabilitation services, legal assistance and enforcement services, as well as repatriation and social reintegration services.

(2) The rights of victims as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be implemented in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.

Part Five

Cooperation

Article 2

The Principles of Protection Implementation for Victims of Gender-Based Violence and Violence Against Children are:

a. non-discrimination;
b. best interests of victims;
c. gender justice and equality;
d. victim protection;
e. maternal survival;
f. survival, growth, and development of children; g. respect for the opinion of children;
h. transparency;
i. integration;
j. not blaming victims;
k. empowerment;
1. victim confidentiality;
m. decision-making in the hands of victims.

Article 36

(1) The community may participate in assisting prevention efforts and handling of victims of gender-based and child violence.

(2) Community participation as referred to in paragraph (1) shall take the form of: a. providing information and/or reporting any violence of which they are aware;

b. providing protection for victims;

c. providing emergency assistance;T 17

d. providing advocacy to victims and/or the community regarding the handling of gender-based and child violence;

e. assisting in the process of submitting applications for protection orders; f. assisting in the process of repatriation and social reintegration.

(3) Community participation as referred to in paragraph (1) may be carried out by individuals, social community institutions, non-governmental organizations, educational institutions, religious institutions, private sector, and mass media.

